      "source": [
        "def plot_enriched_segments_by_jamfactor(gdf, zoom_start=16):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Plot HERE+OSM segments with color by jamFactor and detailed popup.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        gdf (GeoDataFrame): must contain 'jamFactor' and geometry\n",
        "        zoom_start (int): folium zoom level\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    if gdf.empty or \"jamFactor\" not in gdf.columns:\n",
        "        print(\"GeoDataFrame is empty or missing jamFactor.\")\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "\n",
        "    center = gdf.unary_union.centroid\n",
        "    m = folium.Map(location=[center.y, center.x], zoom_start=zoom_start)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Color scale for jamFactor (0 = free flow, 10 = heavy congestion)\n",
        "    colormap = cm.LinearColormap([\"green\", \"yellow\", \"orange\", \"red\"], vmin=0, vmax=10)\n",
        "    colormap.caption = \"Jam Factor\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    for _, row in gdf.iterrows():\n",
        "        jf = row.get(\"jamFactor\")\n",
        "        if jf is not None:\n",
        "            color = colormap(jf)\n",
        "            coords = [(lat, lon) for lon, lat in row.geometry.coords]\n",
        "\n",
        "            popup_html = (\n",
        "                f\"<b>Road:</b> {row.get('roadName', 'Unknown')}<br>\"\n",
        "                f\"<b>Current Speed:</b> {row.get('currentSpeed', 'n/a')}<br>\"\n",
        "                f\"<b>Free Flow Speed:</b> {row.get('freeFlowSpeed', 'n/a')}<br>\"\n",
        "                f\"<b>Jam Factor:</b> {jf}<br>\"\n",
        "                f\"<b>OSM Type:</b> {row.get('highway', 'Unknown')}\"\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "            folium.PolyLine(\n",
        "                locations=coords,\n",
        "                color=color,\n",
        "                weight=5,\n",
        "                popup=folium.Popup(popup_html, max_width=300)\n",
        "            ).add_to(m)\n",
        "\n",
        "    colormap.add_to(m)\n",
        "    return m\n",
        "\n",
        "plot_enriched_segments_by_jamfactor(enriched_gdf)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Clustering Approach\n",
        "\n",
        "Two unsupervised clustering approaches were evaluated: DBSCAN and K-Means.\n",
        "\n",
        "DBSCAN was initially explored because of its ability to identify spatially dense groups without specifying the number of clusters in advance. However, the resulting clusters were not well suited to separating roadway segments according to interpretable congestion states.\n",
        "\n",
        "K-Means was therefore selected for the final analysis because it produced more interpretable groups based on traffic and roadway characteristics."
      ]
    },
