        "def dbscan_with_highway(gdf, eps=200, min_samples=2):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Apply DBSCAN clustering using location, jamFactor, and road type.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "        gdf (GeoDataFrame): must contain 'jamFactor' and 'highway'\n",
        "        eps (float): distance threshold (in meters)\n",
        "        min_samples (int): minimum samples per cluster\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        GeoDataFrame with added 'dbscan_cluster' label\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    df = gdf.dropna(subset=[\"jamFactor\", \"highway\"]).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Ordinal encoding of highway types\n",
        "    highway_types = df[\"highway\"].astype(str).unique()\n",
        "    highway_map = {h: i for i, h in enumerate(sorted(highway_types))}\n",
        "    df[\"highway_encoded\"] = df[\"highway\"].astype(str).map(highway_map)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Reproject to meters\n",
        "    df_proj = df.to_crs(epsg=3857)\n",
        "    df_proj[\"x\"] = df_proj.geometry.centroid.x\n",
        "    df_proj[\"y\"] = df_proj.geometry.centroid.y\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Prepare features\n",
        "    df_proj[\"jamFactor_scaled\"] = df_proj[\"jamFactor\"] * 2.0\n",
        "    df_proj[\"highway_encoded_scaled\"] = df_proj[\"highway_encoded\"] * 1.5\n",
        "\n",
        "    X = df_proj[[\"x\", \"y\", \"jamFactor\", \"highway_encoded\"]].values\n",
        "    X_scaled = StandardScaler().fit_transform(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Apply DBSCAN\n",
        "    db = DBSCAN(eps=eps, min_samples=min_samples).fit(X_scaled)\n",
        "    df[\"dbscan_cluster\"] = db.labels_\n",
        "\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run DBSCAN using both jam factor and road type\n",
        "clustered_enriched_gdf = dbscan_with_highway(enriched_gdf, eps=75, min_samples=3)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check how many segments per cluster\n",
        "clustered_enriched_gdf[\"dbscan_cluster\"].value_counts()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Feature Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "Traffic and roadway characteristics were transformed into features suitable for clustering.\n",
        "\n",
        "The primary congestion indicators were:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Jam Factor** — HERE traffic congestion measure\n",
        "- **Speed Ratio** — current speed divided by free-flow speed\n",
        "- **Road Class** — encoded OpenStreetMap highway classification\n",
        "- **Spatial Location** — roadway segment coordinates\n",
        "\n",
        "Features were standardized using `StandardScaler` before clustering so that differences in measurement scale would not dominate the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "Traffic-related features were weighted more heavily than spatial characteristics to emphasize observed roadway conditions while retaining geographic context."
      ]
    },
